I've left out both operations requests. This node's world imports only `aap:caps/state-read`, so it has no capability for writing a log file or making outbound HTTP calls, and `wasm32-unknown-unknown` provides neither. Adding those imports would widen the node's authority beyond what the graph declares. The metadata request would also send untrusted feed text to an external host. Logging and enrichment need their own declared capabilities, such as a scoped `http-client` handle or a separate node, approved at the graph level.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

